<title>UK: Limelight sets first-day premium.</title>
<headline>Limelight sets first-day premium.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in home improvements products company Limelight Group Plc set a modest premium on their first day of trading on the London Stock Exchange on Friday.</p>
<p>The shares were quoted at 177-1/2p at 1032 GMT, a modest premium to their placing price of 175p, with over five million shares changing hands.</p>
<p>Limelight was valued at 175 million stg at the offer price.</p>
<p>&quot;It is a good company and I believe the prices will go up,&quot; said one industry analyst, who declined to be named.</p>
<p>--Lewa Pardomuan, London Newsroom ++44 171 542 7945</p>
